              "text": "In a maths lesson Jamie drew some triangles and some quadrilaterals.",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "break"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "He drew 27 polygons altogether and a total of 99 vertices. How many triangles did he draw?",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "9 triangles. Let $x$ be the number of triangles: $3x+4(27-x)=99$.",
      "worked": {
        "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
        "version": 1,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "id": "p19-q16-answer",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "right",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Let ",
                "marks": [],
                "colour": "#268cff"
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "x",
                "display": false,
                "colour": "#268cff"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": " be the number of triangles, so ",
                "marks": [],
                "colour": "#268cff"
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "27-x",
                "display": false,
                "colour": "#268cff"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": " is the number of quadrilaterals.",
                "marks": [],
                "colour": "#268cff"
              },
              {
                "type": "break"
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "\\begin{aligned}3x+4(27-x)&=99\\\\3x+108-4x&=99\\\\-x+108&=99\\\\-x&=-9\\\\x&=9\\end{aligned}",
                "display": false,
                "colour": "#268cff"
              },
              {
                "type": "break"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Jamie drew 9 triangles.",
